Work continues apace on the Alchemist class. I've decided that the gods
will be:

Lawful: Sol
Neutral: Terra
Chaotic: Luna

as they don't overlap with the others and are nicely 'scientific'.

I like the idea of having a polymorphing Jekyll/Hyde character as the
quest nemesis, but I'm having trouble choosing a quest leader. There
have been a number of good suggestions -- Parcellus, John Dee, Roger
Bacon, Isaac Newton -- but none of them are even vaguely
contemporaneous with the Jekyll/Hyde story (set in the late 1800s). I
don't imagine many people would care, but the anachronism bugs me.

I _could_ use le Comte de St Germain, he lived in the 1700s, but he was
reputed to be an immortal, so he could still be around. Actually, that
gives me an idea....

